The vertex shader of dEQP-GLES2.functional.uniform_api.value.assigned.{by_pointer,by_value}.render.basic_struct.sampler2D_samplerCube_vertex (plan #406 item vs2tex-ref, issue #11308), rebuilt from VK-GL-CTS 93bca01 modules/gles2/functional/es2fUniformApiTests.cpp (UniformCase::generateVertexSource, writeUniformDefinitions, writeUniformComparisons, UniformCollection::basicStruct); the two fill colours are de::Random(deStringHash("sampler2D_samplerCube_vertex")) at base seed 0, as UniformCase::iterate draws them. Its fragment shader is vs_tex2d_cube.frag. Mesa 26.2.1 does not draw it through tools/mali/gl_ref.py (a sampler struct member is not set, so both samplers stay at unit 0 and the draw is GL_INVALID_OPERATION); its NIR and disassembly at the link are those of vs_tex2d_cube.vert, the same text with the two members as plain uniforms (tests/mali_vs_tex2d_cube.rs).
